<title>UK: Nightfreight slumps on profit warning.</title>
<headline>Nightfreight slumps on profit warning.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nightfreight Plc on Friday plunged by almost one third after the parcel and freight group disclosed its result for the year would be below expectations.</p>
<p>&quot;They clearly slumped on the news&quot;, one trader said, referring to the profit warning from Nightfreight.</p>
<p>By 0850 GMT, Nightfreight was down 13-1/2p to 28-1/2.</p>
<p>The company said in its trading statement it was currently trading below budget level and the new palletisation system Genesis was more costly than expected.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
